<description>
Extract the color of each noisy block in a row/column lattice and mirror the coarse grid horizontally.

Input structure:
- A background surrounds a rectangular lattice of monochrome foreground blocks.
- Consecutive rows in a lattice band share the same set of visible foreground colors.
- Consecutive columns in a lattice band share the same set of visible foreground colors.
- Each row-band/column-band intersection has one foreground color, with possible background holes.

Rule:
- Group non-empty rows and columns into consecutive bands by their foreground color sets.
- Replace each lattice cell by the single foreground color inside that row/column-band intersection.
- Return the resulting coarse color grid with the column order reversed.

Key insight:
- Whole-row and whole-column color sets reveal the hidden lattice even when neighboring cells share a color or contain holes.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "move_in_order",
  "src": "row/column-band intersections s ordered by row band top-to-bottom and column band right-to-left",
  "dst": "coarse output cells d ordered row-major",
  "match_cond": "rank(s) == rank(d)",
  "transform": "collapse each s to its single foreground color",
  "grid_shape": "output is the coarse lattice size"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 18-22 rows x 11-19 cols, bg=0
  lattice:
    description: rectangular block of fg pixels surrounded by >=1 row/col of bg on all sides
    coarse_dims: 2-4 row bands x 2-3 col bands
    band_height: 3-8 rows per band
    band_width: 3-6 cols per band
    total_fg_area: 8-16 rows x 8-14 cols (sum of band dims)
  cells:
    each row-band x col-band intersection is filled with exactly one fg color
    colors 1-9, total distinct colors = 4-8
    colors MAY repeat across cells (so distinct count < row_bands * col_bands is allowed)
  band_detection_constraint:
    every row within a band has identical fg color set (union of cell colors in that row)
    adjacent bands must have different color sets
    same applies to columns
  holes:
    5-20% of pixels within each cell are bg (holes), rest are the cell's color
    holes placed so that every row in a band still contains all band colors
    and every column in a band still contains all band colors
  output:
    coarse_grid[r,c] = cell color at (row_band r, col_band c) with columns REVERSED
    output size = n_row_bands x n_col_bands

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. pick coarse dims R in [2,4], C in [2,3]; pick R*C cell colors (from 1-9, repeats ok, 4-8 distinct total)
    2. assign colors to coarse grid; derive row-band color sets and col-band color sets; verify adjacent bands differ
    3. pick band heights (3-8 each) and widths (3-6 each) to form the lattice
    4. fill each cell region with its color, then sprinkle bg holes (5-20% per cell)
    5. after placing holes, verify every row in each band still has all band colors and every col in each band still has all band colors; if not, remove offending holes
    6. embed lattice in a larger grid with >=1 bg padding on each side
    7. output = coarse color grid with columns reversed
